course: dictionary
lesson: 10126
title: A thousand, and thousands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thousand is the number 1,000, which is ten hundreds. «J, U and W were added to English only in the last thousand years.» Here thousand is an exact count: a thousand years is 1,000 years.
explain: Thousands can also mean a very large number that nobody has counted exactly. «A family of barn owls can eat over a thousand mice and voles in a year.» Over a thousand means more than 1,000, and the exact amount is not given.
explain: «People in the Andes tamed guinea pigs thousands of years ago.» Thousands of years does not mean exactly 3,000 years. It means a very long time, so you can tell the word is about size, not an exact number. Ask yourself: is the writer counting exactly, or showing how big something is?
fact: A thousand is written 1,000, with a comma to help us read it.
fact: Ten hundreds make a thousand, so 10 × 100 = 1,000.
fact: In the number 4,326, the 4 means four thousands.
fact: «Thousands of» means a very large number that is not counted exactly.
fact: A kilometre is a thousand metres, and a kilogram is a thousand grams.
exercise: «The team walked a thousand metres to the lake.» What does a thousand mean here? | One hundred metres | *1,000 metres, exactly | A few metres, about ten | Lots of metres, but nobody counted them
exercise: «Thousands of ants crawled across the path.» What does thousands mean here? | Exactly one thousand and one | Exactly one | Exactly ten | *A very large number, not counted exactly
exercise: In the number 4,326, what does the 4 mean? | *four thousands | forty | four ones | four hundreds
test: «Jesus fed five thousand people with a boy's five loaves and two fish.» How many people is five thousand? | 500 | 50 | *5,000 | Nobody knows
test: Which phrase means a very large number, not counted exactly? | Ten hundreds | A thousand metres | One thousand pages | *Thousands of stars
exam: Which number is a thousand written with digits? | 100 | 10,000 | *1,000 | 1,100
